  "subject": "syzygy-pdja.33 identity widening to 046's grammar in every reader (cd303259..5ef9dabd)",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "note": "Rule-6 mutants for the owner's ruling of 2026-11-14, 'Widen all readers now', each section at its own commit; readers were widened before the writer (IDENTITY), so no commit writes an identity a reader refuses. Each mutant was applied alone, the named test files run, and the file restored byte-identical. Sweep: git grep -nE over packages, apps and scripts (tests and fixtures excluded) for 'repository:' followed by a character class or capture, repositoryId tested by a regex, or '[a-z0-9][a-z0-9': 14 hit lines, of which 8 read a repository identity; the other 6 read provider, project, tag, walkthrough, evaluation or campaign keys. A second sweep over all 118 non-test lines naming 'repository:' found no further reader. Not widened: scripts/differential_consent_act_families.mjs:837, an evidence tool that reads the two fixed instance files to set a probe and gates nothing. Each mutant set includes a case-insensitive or folding variant (W2, W5, X2, X5, Y2, Z2, V2, I4), killed, so no reader merges two repositories by case or by '.', '_' and '-'.",
